/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 68 0 R
/T (Today, there is not a single nation on Earth without some sort of educational system, and for most young people worldwide, the quality or quantity of the education they receive in school will significantly impact their chances of success as adults. The developing world lags developed countries by around a century when considering average education years and attainment levels. And unfortunately, the current educational techniques will likely result in this century-long divide persisting into the future. An innovative approach such as immersive VR, emerges as a natural successor in reshaping education and bridging the persistent global education gap.)
/E (Today, there is not a single nation on Earth without some sort of educational system, and for most young people worldwide, the quality or quantity of the education they receive in school will significantly impact their chances of success as adults. The developing world lags developed countries by around a century when considering average education years and attainment levels. And unfortunately, the current educational techniques will likely result in this century-long divide persisting into the future. An innovative approach such as immersive VR, emerges as a natural successor in reshaping education and bridging the persistent global education gap.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
